<title>USA: Northrop units secures $9.4 mln contract.</title>
<headline>Northrop units secures $9.4 mln contract.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Northrop Grumman Corp said Wednesday its Electronic Sensors and Systems division and GDE Systems unit have secured a $9.4 million U.S. Army contract.</p>
<p>The contract is to develop the handheld standoff mine detection system. The contract calls for the team to develop and deliver 10 systems over the next 30 months.</p>
<p>The system is able to detect buried mines from greater than 10 feet away.</p>
</text>
